Reverted by known_bugs.sh to reintroduce the bug fixed by 643e1bed9:
voice core: a host interrupt() that races the speech's end lands, as the reference's does
Re-cut against the ordered host requests: the runtime steps every request the host made of its
speeches before the input that could end one (Runtime::step); reverted, a request waits for its
own wake in the queue and lands behind an end queued ahead of it.

diff --git a/rust/crates/lk-agents-runtime/src/voice/mod.rs b/rust/crates/lk-agents-runtime/src/voice/mod.rs
--- a/rust/crates/lk-agents-runtime/src/voice/mod.rs
+++ b/rust/crates/lk-agents-runtime/src/voice/mod.rs
@@ -298,8 +298,11 @@
     /// `interrupt()` asked while the host still read it running lands first. The list stays
     /// locked until the step's views are published: a later request reads the speech's end.
     fn step(&mut self, input: Option<Input>, now: Now) {
+        let requests = self.shared.speeches.requests(self.reports.clone());
+        let held = self.step_host_requests_from(&requests, now);
         let effects = self.driver.handle(input, now);
         let operations = self.publish_views(effects);
+        drop(held);
         self.operate(operations);
     }
 
